10153	{"artifactId":"LLD-2764c29d7ccb66a5-s1","entry":{"id":"migrated-LLD-2764c29d7ccb66a5-s1-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:daemon","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-10T15:17:06.985Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"pass","summary":"review: pass","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"pass","findings":[{"claimId":"fix-targets-defect.1","ref":"fix-targets-defect","item":"fix-targets-defect","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The root cause is that nothing compares the index with the disk or the ignore list: entities of a file are removed only on the watcher's delete event, so a clean-up pass at daemon start and inside a full index covers the ISSUE's fix intent (deleted files, newly ignored directories, relations and vectors, no re-registration).","evidence":"src/indexer/index.ts: fullIndex (360-497) and detectDelta (294-316) only list files via `listRepoFiles(repoPath, resolveRepoIgnore(repoPath))` and index them; neither reads the stored entities. The only file-level removals are in fileEvent `if (event === 'delete')` (513-516) and indexFile's cleanFirst branch (763-765). The ignore rule the design reuses exists as `hasIgnoredSegment` (97-99: `relative(repoPath, file).split(sep).some(seg => ignoreSet.has(seg))`), a whole-segment compare, in the same file as the new pass. ISSUE.md fix intent ('brought to that state when the daemon next indexes it', relations and vectors removed) is met by the start-up reconcile job plus the full-index call; `repo.reindex` only enqueues `{ kind: 'full' }` (src/daemon/index.ts:811-818), so it is covered too. [files: src/indexer/index.ts, src/daemon/index.ts, docs/standalone/index-never-reconciled-against-files-disk-E202610102764c29d/ISSUE.md]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The watcher's file deletes match a path in every repository, so reusing them would remove a nested registered repository's entities.","evidence":"src/db/entities.ts:1016-1027 `collectEntityU64sByFileInTxn` ranges over the whole `store.entity` table and matches `toAbsolutePath(row.filePath, repoPath) === file` with no repo filter. src/db/relations.ts:312-336 `deleteUnresolvedForFile` loops `for (const repoId of repos)` over every registered repo ('we scan all repos'). `deleteRelationsForFile` (197-201) is an empty body, so it adds nothing. [files: src/db/entities.ts, src/db/relations.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"At daemon start a repository left `indexing` with a last-indexed time gets no job, and a `ready` one gets only mtime-delta file jobs.","evidence":"src/indexer/index.ts:241-268: full job only for `pending`, `error`, or `(repo.status === 'indexing' && !repo.lastIndexed)`; the only other branch is `else if (repo.status === 'ready' && repo.lastIndexed)` which runs detectDelta and enqueues `{ kind: 'file', ..., event: 'update' }`. `indexing` with lastIndexed falls through both. [files: src/indexer/index.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.3","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"fileEvent and indexFile never consult the ignore list, and the daemon's `index.file` request enqueues a file job for any path; the file's repository is the longest registered prefix.","evidence":"src/indexer/index.ts:499-530 (fileEvent) and 741-800 (indexFile) contain no call to resolveRepoIgnore or hasIgnoredSegment. src/daemon/index.ts:1344-1348: `queue.enqueue({ kind: 'file', filePath, event: event ?? 'update' })` with no path check. repoForFile (993-1004) picks `if (root.length > best.length) best = root`, so a file in a nested registered repo is judged against the child's ignore list, not the parent's; the new guard does not block the child's files. [files: src/indexer/index.ts, src/daemon/index.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The change sites named (src/shared/types.ts, src/daemon/queue.ts, src/indexer/index.ts, src/db/entities.ts, src/db/relations.ts) are the complete set of code that switches on the job kind or must learn the new job, and the existing unresolved index supports a per-repository, per-file removal.","evidence":"Grep for `job.kind` over src/, vscode-plugin/src and jetbrains-plugin/src finds only src/indexer/index.ts:344 (processJob switch, no default and no never-check) and src/daemon/queue.ts (depthForRepo switch with a bare `default: break`, and the enqueue dedup chain). IndexJob is declared at src/shared/types.ts:704. depthForRepo has one consumer, src/daemon/repo-stats.ts:163. IndexerService is constructed once in production, src/daemon/index.ts:276, with four arguments, so a further optional constructor argument breaks no caller. The index the new removal reads exists: src/db/relations.ts:270-271 maintains `encodeUnresolvedByFileKey(repoId, row.fromFile)` and line 325 reads it per repoId. Note: section 3.2 says both that the removal is 'a direct read of the existing index by repository and file' and that such an index 'would make it a direct read; this design does not need it'. The second sentence can only be about the entity read (ISSUE-61045de9); as written it contradicts the first. [files: src/daemon/queue.ts, src/indexer/index.ts, src/shared/types.ts, src/db/relations.ts, src/daemon/repo-stats.ts]","action":"Move the ISSUE-61045de9 sentence in section 3.2 so it qualifies listEntityFilesForRepo, not deleteUnresolvedForRepoFile. Since the processJob switch has no exhaustiveness check and depthForRepo has a bare default, keep the tests that call processJob and depthForRepo with the new kind.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"preserved-behaviour.1","ref":"preserved-behaviour","item":"preserved-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"deleteEntitiesById ends in the same single cascade as the watcher's delete (edges, name index entries, vectors), keyed by explicit ids, so the clean-up adds no second cascade and touches only the ids it passes.","evidence":"src/db/entities.ts:549-558: deleteEntitiesById maps each id with lookupU64ByStringId and calls `detachDeleteEntities(store, u64s)`, the same function deleteEntitiesForFile calls at 525. detachDeleteEntities (1048-1063) runs detachDeleteEntitiesInTxn in one write txn (sweepOutgoingEdges, sweepIncomingEdges, deleteDocSummaryInTxn, nameIndex.remove, id-map removes, entity.remove) and then `deleteEntityVecsByIds(stringIds)`. That it always imports the Lance module matches the design's note that every removing test must set the vector store path. Already used the same way at src/indexer/external-endpoints.ts:185. [files: src/db/entities.ts, src/indexer/external-endpoints.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"preserved-behaviour.2","ref":"preserved-behaviour","item":"preserved-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A full index already puts the cached exploration results out of use by stamping a new last-indexed time, while a stand-alone clean-up does not, so it must call deleteCachedExplorationsForRepo, which removes one repository's rows only.","evidence":"src/db/exploration-cache.ts:14-16: key is `<repoId u32 BE>|<repoLastIndexedAt ms u64 BE>|<paramHash>` 'so a re-index invalidates every cached exploration for that repo automatically'; fullIndex stamps `updateRepoStatus(this.db, repoPath, 'ready', new Date().toISOString())` at src/indexer/index.ts:485. At start the stamp is renewed only when the delta is non-empty (264), so a reconcile on an unchanged repo would otherwise leave the cache live. deleteCachedExplorationsForRepo (159-173) removes the range from the repoId prefix to repoId + 1 and nothing of another repo. [files: src/db/exploration-cache.ts, src/indexer/index.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each acceptance criterion maps to a test that fails without the fix, and the named existing test file and store seams exist.","evidence":"src/daemon/__tests__/queue-depth-for-repo.test.ts enqueues every current kind (full, reembed, doc-summarise-repo, file, config-file, config-full, config-reindex, doc-summarise-entity); with today's queue a `reconcile` job hits `default: break` (depthForRepo returns 0) and is not deduplicated, so the ac3 queue test fails without the change. `setGraphStorePath` (src/db/graph/store.ts:273) and `setLanceConnPath` (src/db/lance/conn.ts:42) exist. The ac1/ac2/ac4 integration subjects assert removals and non-removals that today's code cannot produce (no code path removes an entity of an absent or ignored file outside a watcher delete). Gaps that are not acceptance criteria but are stated behaviour without a named test: the 2.2 postcondition that a failed clean-up marks the repository `error`, and the ordering of the clean-up before the cross-file resolver inside a full index. Also `settleTimers` is a private field (src/indexer/index.ts:162), so 'leaves no settle timer armed' needs an observable seam the design does not name. [files: src/daemon/__tests__/queue-depth-for-repo.test.ts, src/daemon/queue.ts, src/indexer/index.ts]","action":"Add a test subject for a clean-up failure inside a full index leaving the repository `error`, and say how the test observes that no settle timer is armed (for example, a short settleWindowMs and a check that the resolver did not run a second time).","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":0,"low":8,"unverified":0},"template":"design-issue","reviewedAt":"2026-10-10T15:17:06.985Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
